  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nI propose a novel approach using Multi-Swarm Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) combined with directional coordinate descent. This method addresses the limitations of previous local optimization techniques by using:\n- Multiple swarms to explore different regions of the sequence space\n- Dirac tuning to target specific peak locations in the auto-convolution\n- Recursive direction optimization to automatically identify critical optimization dimensions\n\nThe core idea is to decompose the optimization problem into its critical dimensions where improvements in auto-convolution have the most significant impact. This reduces the effective problem size while maintaining optimality guarantees, leveraging directional properties of the step function.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\nFor a sequence `a` of length `n`:\n\nLet `f(a) = 2*n*max(conv(a,a,mode='full'))/(sum(a))^2`\nWith nonnegativity constraints `\u2200i \u2208 [0, n), 0 \u2264 a_i \u2264 1000`\n\nObjective: find `argmin` `f(a)`\n\nKey components:\n1. Directed derivative computation:  \n   `conv(a,a)[k] = sum_{i+j=k} a[i] * a[j]`\n   Contribution to gradient depends only on the sign at `k` and its value\n2. Dimension prioritization: optimized to automatically identify directions with maximum curvature\n3. Multiple swarms: independent optimization processes targeting different structural configurations\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\ndef build_conv_matrix(n):\n    return np.zeros((2*n-1, n))\n\ndef coordinate_optimization(a, iterations=100):\n    dims = len(a)\n    best_score = np.inf\n    best_coords = None\n    \n    for i in range(10, dims//2):\n        # Compute gradient on current dimension\n        conv_val = compute_gradient_contribution(a, i) * compute_gradient_contribution(a, dims-1-i)\n        if conv_val > 1e-10:\n            # Optimize only this dimension\n            def obj_func(x):\n                new_a = a.copy()\n                new_a[i] = x[0]\n                new_a[dims-1-i] = x[1] / x[0] * a[dims-1-i]  # Scale to maintain same structure\n                return evaluate_sequence(new_a.tolist()) if np.isfinite(sum(new_a)) else np.inf\n            try:\n                res = minimize(obj_func, [a[i], a[dims-1-i]], bounds=[(0,1000), (0,1000)], method='L-BFGS-B')\n                candidate_score = obj_func(res.x)\n                if candidate_score < best_score:\n                    best_score = candidate_score\n                    best_coords = res.x\n                    # Preserve current weights naturally\n                    best_weights = best_coords[0] * a[dims-1-i] / best_coords[1] if best_coords[1] > 0 else 0\n                    best_coords_scl = [best_coords[0] * (a[i]/1000), best_coords[1] * (a[i]/1000)]\n            except:\n                pass\n            \n    optimal_dims = determine_optimal_dimensions(a)\n    return optimize_directions(a, optimal_dims)\n```\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n```python:\nprior_hyper_params = {\n    'psize': (10, None),  # Keep typical PSO inertia\n    'alpha': (0.8, 0.99),  # Shift focus from distance to goal\n    'beta': (0.3, 0.95),  # Local search weight variation\n    'nswarms': (5, 10)   # Number of independent optimization streams\n}\n```\n\n5. Budget Allocation\n```python\ndef setup_budget_allocation(deadline):\n    budget = {\n        'swarm': {'max_seq_len': 800, 'time_ratio': 0.6, 'iters_limit': 500},\n        'conv_size': (4, 8),  # Balance between coarse and fine checks\n        'progress_step': 0.0001\n    }\n    return budget\n```\n\n6. Full Implementation Plan\n```python\ndef evaluate_sequence(sequence):\n    # Safety-critical validation of provided sequence\n    ...\n\ndef make_cosine(n):\n    # Amplitude normalized cosine sequence\n    return np.zeros(n)\n\ndef make_parabolic(n):\n    # Parabolic taper sequence\n    return np.exp(-(np.arange(n) - (n-1)/2 - 0.5)**2 * n^2)\n\ndef propose_candidate(seed=42, budget_s=1800):\n    print(\"Initializing Multi-Swarm Optimization strategy\")\n    \n    # Dynamic configuration\n    conf = setup_budget_allocation(budget_s)\n    \n    # Base PSO parameters\n    base_psize = conf['psize'][0]\n    base_alpha = conf['alpha'][0]\n    base_beta_low = conf['beta'][0]\n    base_beta_high = conf['beta'][1]\n    \n    # Prioritize dimension-wise optimization\n    optimized_dims = determine_optimal_dimensions()\n    \n    # Initialize best candidate\n    best_seq = np.random.rand(base_psize)  # Placeholder\n    best_score = evaluate_sequence(best_seq.tolist()).item() if np.isfinite(best_score) else np.inf\n    \n    # Swarm parameters\n    swarms = 3\n    pswarm_size = swarms * base_psize\n    \n    # Centralized inertia control\n    dim_history = {}\n    for d in range(optimized_dims):\n        dim_history[dim] = {'init': None, 'optimizer': None}\n    \n    # Main optimization loop\n    while time.time() < budget_s - 30:\n        print(f\"Iteration: {len(dim_history)}\")\n        for d in optimized_dims:\n            positions = [make_cosine(len) for len in range(psize)]\n            # Compute bounds at all dimensions\n            bounds = get_bounds_for_direction(dim_history[d])\n            result = optimize_with_history(bounds, d)\n            score = evaluate_sequence(result)\n            if score < best_score:\n                best_score = score\n                best_seq = result\n        # Adaptive heuristic\n        relaxation = get_relaxation(self-consistent peaks)\n        candidate = generate_with_optimal_peaks(relaxation)\n        new_score = evaluate_sequence(candidate)\n        if new_score < best_score:\n            best_score = new_score\n            best_seq = candidate\n    \n    # Final validation passes\n    print(\"Performing local optimizers...\")\n    best_seq = local_search(best_seq)\n    print(f\"Optimizing final candidate with extrapolation...\")\n    best_seq = ensure_complete_dirac_minimization(best_seq)\n    \n    return best_seq.tolist()\n```\n\nThe implementation will include structured pre-conditioning, dimension-aware execution blending, and consistent score validation with the original objective",
